<title>UK: St Lawrence seaway reopens as wheat ship refloats.</title>
<headline>St Lawrence seaway reopens as wheat ship refloats.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two-way traffic resumed on the St. Lawrence seaway on June 22 after the Canadian-flag wheat carrier Canadian Mariner was refloated, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence Service said on Monday.</p>
<p>The 27,350 dwt vessel refloated four days after it ran aground, during which time steering problems were repaired.</p>
<p>The bulker was carrying 25,000 tonnes of wheat from Thunder Bay, Ontario, to Quebec City and about 2,500 tonnes had to be unloaded because of the repairs.</p>
